{
 "method": "Custom photon Monte Carlo (2.5e6 source photons) with the beam defined as a square pyramid (10x10 cm2 at surface, SSD 100 cm, source in vacuum) transporting photons in the 30 cm water cube using XCOM interaction data (incoherent/coherent/photo/pair). Fluence at the 5 cm scoring cylinder (r=1 cm, t=0.2 cm) was scored with a next-flight track-length estimator, giving primary/scattered fluence, 28-bin and angular spectra, and depth profiles. Interaction fractions and electron-initial spectra follow from fluence x cross sections with Klein-Nishina kinematics. Electron fluence was obtained from the CSDA equilibrium spectrum (ESTAR stopping powers) plus one-generation Moller delta rays; dose = collision kerma x transient-equilibrium factor from a 1-D electron-kernel convolution; PDD from the resulting depth-dose profile. Spencer-Attix water/air ratio used ESTAR water and Bethe-formula air stopping powers (Delta=10 keV, track-end included).",
 "data_sources": "NIST XCOM water photon mass-attenuation coefficients (cm2/g vs MeV) by process; NIST ESTAR water electron stopping powers, CSDA range and radiation yields; air collision stopping powers computed with the Bethe formula (I=85.7 eV, Z/A=0.4993).",
